{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima and Lateralus feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want to hear more of Tool's intricate rhythms and atmospheric, extended songs.",
    "City of Evil appeals to me because its melodic guitar work combines the heavy energy and tunefulness I enjoy across my recent listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Futureperfect's electronic direction misses the guitar-driven music I want right now, even if it shares a dark mood with some of my listening.",
    "St. Anger, God Hates Us All, and Iowa fit my interest in heavy music, but raw aggression or relentless intensity is less appealing today than melody and progressive songwriting."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in heavy albums seems to have been taken as a reason to offer more aggression, although heaviness alone does not make something a priority for me.",
    "A dark or brooding mood seems to have counted too much as a shared quality when the instruments and songwriting matter more to my choices."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interaction with 10.000 Days makes exploring more Tool especially compelling this visit.",
    "I want heaviness with memorable melodies or complex rhythms; several albums fit my broader taste without being ones I would choose today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my heavy rock and metal interests, but only some capture my current preference for Tool, intricate songwriting, and melodic heaviness."
}"}
